            "advisory": "Affected versions of the PyJWKClient package are vulnerable to Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) due to a missing scheme allowlist. The `uri` argument is passed directly to `urllib.request.urlopen()`, which by default supports multiple URI schemes including `file://`, `ftp://`, and `data:`, without restriction. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by providing a crafted `jku` URL, potentially leading to unauthorized file reads or token forgery if they have write access to a filesystem path and can control the URL.",
